 ('LOM805-04','Not-recommended vs formal contraindication conflated','The prior numeric renal rule labelledCrCl<30/dialysis as contraindicated.','Preserve NCCP not-recommended wording with an administration hold; separately encode the product formal severe-renal-impairment contraindication. Review30–50 original-dose75% against dose history rather than automatically multiplying the current dose.','NCCP p2 Table2; SmPC p2'),
 ('LOM805-05','Missing minimum interval and exposure limits','No executable repeat-interval, course cap, dose-intensity or cumulative exposure check.','Structured single-doseDay1q42 schedule;280mg cap; proposed>130mg/m², repeat<42days and projected>1000mg/m² restrictions. Existing≥1000mg/m² prevents further courses. Missing exposure is not zero.','NCCP p1; SmPC pp1–3'),
 ('LOM805-06','Delayed nadirs not assessed','Only current ANC/platelets were encoded.','Add priorWBC/platelet nadirs with source-labelled review; distinguishANCfromWBC, retain prior reductions, flag current SmPC repeat-doseWBC≥4 requirement. No automatic percentage from discordant/overlapping table rows.','SmPC p2'),
 ('LOM805-07','Product nadir-table overlap','Current SmPC70% platelet row starts at24,000/mm³, overlapping50% row below25,000.','Explicit24–<25×10⁹/L overlap warning; all nadir percentages require consultant/pharmacy reconciliation.','SmPC p2 nadir table'),
 ('LOM805-08','Nonhaematological reduction/restoration history missing','A single active Grade≥3 rule included reduction and possible later restoration without verifying recovery, recurrence, dose history or42days.','Separate active hold, history, baseline recovery, clinical relevance, already-applied reduction and42-day nonrecurrence review; no calculated50% or full-dose restoration.','NCCP p3 Table3'),
 ('LOM805-09','Missing product contraindications','No direct flags for other nitrosourea allergy/nonresponse, severe marrow depression, product-specific wheat allergy or live vaccines.','Add source-labelled exclusions, including careful distinction of wheat allergy from coeliac disease and supplier-specific product excipients.','SmPC p2 section4.3'),
 ('LOM805-10','Monitoring lacked source separation','No explicit weeklyCBC≥6weeks or PFT source difference.','NCCP baseline/regularFBCrenalLFT retained; current SmPC weeklyCBC for at least six weeks and baseline/frequentPFTs explicit. NCCP PFTs remain described as conditional high-risk testing; individualMRI plan retained.','NCCP p2; SmPC pp2–3'),
 ('LOM805-11','Contraception advice outdated relative to supplied product reference','NCCP says6months for both men/women; January2026 common SmPC says7women/4men.','Both positions clearly identified for pharmacy/product confirmation; do not silently shorten existing advice or claim a common universal duration.','NCCP p3; SmPC p4'),
